{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Power Method.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Power Method.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"power method power method","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Power Method.md","fileName":"Power Method.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Power Method","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 00:13\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Matrix and Vector Computation]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Matrix and Vector Computation","Vector","Matrix","Eigenvector","PageRank Vector","Dominant Eigenvalue","Rayleigh Quotient","algorithms.epub","appliedlinearalgebraandoptimizationusingmatlab.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Power Method.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Power Method.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"power method power method","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Power Method.md","fileName":"Power Method.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Power Method","heading":"Power Method","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The power method starts with a [[Vector]] and repeatedly multiplies it by the same [[Matrix]]. Under the required conditions, the successive vectors converge toward the matrix's leading [[Eigenvector]].\n\nPageRank begins with relative-importance values summing to one and repeatedly applies the Google matrix. When another iteration no longer changes the [[PageRank Vector]], the stable values provide the final ranking.\n\nFor a general matrix, each multiplication is normally followed by normalization to prevent overflow and expose the scale factor. Convergence requires a [[Dominant Eigenvalue]] and a starting vector with a nonzero component in its eigendirection; the [[Rayleigh Quotient]] can estimate the corresponding eigenvalue.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Matrix and Vector Computation","Vector","Matrix","Eigenvector","PageRank Vector","Dominant Eigenvalue","Rayleigh Quotient","algorithms.epub","appliedlinearalgebraandoptimizationusingmatlab.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Power Method.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Power Method.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"power method power method","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Power Method.md","fileName":"Power Method.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Power Method","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[algorithms.epub]]\n\n[[appliedlinearalgebraandoptimizationusingmatlab.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Matrix and Vector Computation","Vector","Matrix","Eigenvector","PageRank Vector","Dominant Eigenvalue","Rayleigh Quotient","algorithms.epub","appliedlinearalgebraandoptimizationusingmatlab.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}